bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:444:!! Stride 1 Spine
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:448:!!! Seven-league stride notes
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:453:* ''Research pair: the far agent's relay seat'' (`I1`'s relay phase). Its question: the least relay trust and attestation that stops capability escalation and argument substitution while keeping causal provenance. Lenses: protocol security / distributed failure semantics.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:455:!!! The rows
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:460:* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. The boot stands (PRs #48 and #61): the vessel lock gives back on a throw and a `sealed-locked` boot retries in the same page, the web boot asks the unlock through its own form, the clear verb answers `asks` and calls no door before a literal yes, the wiki's `tm-clear-password` road asks through TW5's confirm road and writes no synced tiddler, the question names what it clears, and a declined unlock retries in the page. Under #/rulings (a shared act never makes a shared secret) the browser holds no vessel key, so the clear names one face and clears that face's rows, built inside `K15` steps 0 through 3. Owed: the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">>). Built with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, an unadmitted port asking for a sealed body refusing by name, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive; the production holder lifecycle stays a named skip on every engine until Wave C's one SharedWorker per house. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:461:* `W4` The face-scoped proof chain: face key, the vessel's face key, the session key. The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the session face supplier stand specified in code, and the withdrawal proof reads as a house model the operator may overturn (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>). The two custody rows stand in node (`face-key-custody.ts`); fleet join calls the certificate and grant path, and `openJoinedFaceSession` stands. Owed: the browser holder of the face's custody rows. House. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:468:* `K12` A fresh PersonaGroup for a seat no hand can revoke (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>). The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so every other seat's revocation rolls the bags the group reaches (`persona-group-roll`); revoke authority follows the seating lineage, so a seat whose seating hand left, and the founder's own seat, leave only by a fresh group. Owed first: a name the face keeps across groups, since its plane names key on the group's id. It builds inside `K15`'s per-face removal step. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:471:* `G13` Summons: no check of who wrote one; a consume tombstones every layer; dedup lives in memory (`verb-dispatcher.ts`, `verb-summons.ts`). Owed: a writer check, a working-layer tombstone alone, durable dedup, lease and fence, and honouring `aud`. House. G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:472:* `G34` A removal no reader can keep refuses by name (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/automerge-doc-store">>). The store lands a based removal a concurrent writer overrode, then surfaces it to a listening reader alone: with no parallel-drafts reader it drops the surfacing with no word, and a reader that throws earns one console line while the write stands (`automerge-doc-store.ts`, `parallel-drafts.ts`). Owed: the refusal by name before any change lands, wherever no reader stands or every reader failed, with the store authoring no draft of its own; and the durable conflict handle the refusal carries (the document, the removal's request id, the conflicting change and head identities, never the hand's text), at a home where a hand whose editor went offline finds it again. G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:473:* `G35` The disk watcher's standing instruction (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law">>). Owed: the instruction as a record the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag, a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling, which no automated seat signs; the watcher's settle of each pending removal it covers through the shore's removal door; the audit row that names the instruction a removal rode; `lares shore restore` over a settled removal; and a mass vanish past the ceiling, a standoff, or a removal outside the pattern left pending for a person (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`, `shore-verb.ts`, `disk-projector.ts`). G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:481:* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C. The realm leg, K17-R (kit `docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`, the operator's rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22), landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26: one lease law, so a Nexus or realm lease rises only on a charter quorum's signed advance read under its seal-epoch lineage and the unsigned max-register retires with no reader left; each voucher signs its own hand's frontier; a seal roll signs every anchored realm's head under the new epoch; a split-seat cosign carries its head; and the realm admit bundle carries the board's acts, frontiers and snapshots, so a joiner holding no board acts as of them. Owed to `K18`: a closed roster's keys can still raise the lease (stale more, never less) until the recovery door closes that window; the fold never lowers.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:482:* `K18` The recovery door: guardian-quorum rotation of a persona root beneath its KEL prefix, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the current `@persona` log and signed frontier. Owed: no production door rotates a root today, and the ceremony waits on the guardian count, an open operator gate (`kahu#/seed-and-nexus`); `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function (Wave C, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane">> #/owed). K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:487:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:489:* `W12` The herm route for cancel and the three receipts, as ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg">>); no code asks, cancels or answers across a herm. Owed, with `W9`: the ask, the cancel and the vessel's answer as a tagged inner frame under the sealed sibling session's own seal, the vessel reading that session's proof as the asker's; the herm's bare delivery note inside the session, bound to the ask's unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; and the rule for which verbs a sibling's standing reaches across the session (`sibling-channel.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:490:* `E2` The serving key's custody and its unattended road (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Built: the fifth class `serving` in the carrier table, read by the census and `vault status`; SK minted at the founding; `sk-slots` with the vessel key's entry, opened at every human unlock and re-wrapped by a vessel-key rotation. Owed: the serving rows under SK and SK's own rotation; no minting secret in any serving row; the anchor path, where an ember slot answers unattended only against a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; the confirm path, where every slot of a hearth with no such anchor answers only on a person's confirm and threshold two asks a second confirm, never an unattended raise; and the bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark that any counted removal sets and that refuses every ask until SK rolls (`vault-carriers.ts`, `keyslot.ts`, `custody-seat.ts`). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:491:* `E3` The serving gate's tier (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). Owed: a third tier name in the route type, its bundle derived from SK under its own registered domain, its pin, and a pin's move by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step alone, with no quiet period that ages a pin out (`gate-bundle.ts`). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:492:* `E4` The raise's commit point and its lapse (#/rulings, how a raise lapses; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>). Owed: the count spent at the raise ledger's durable commit, before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise; and the raise's lapse at a lock, a restart, a human unlock or a counted removal, with no timer and no heartbeat that ends it (`custody-seat.ts`, the raise ledger's writer). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:493:* `H2` The delegation and three dials stand specified in `hosting-delegation.ts`. Owed: the live issuer, reader, hosting store and socket sorter in one signed-act cut. H.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:494:* `H8` The grant's signed shape and public-half verifier stand specified in `walker-grant.ts` (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-tiers">>). Owed: the live roll that derives grant public halves for serving rows inside H's one act cut, before E's walker arm. H.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:500:!! Stride 2 Floor
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:504:!!! Seven-league stride notes
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:506:* ''Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence). Its witness: a rotation-and-carry storm that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:510:!!! The rows
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:512:* `W14` The floor card a banner carries in its `#floor=` link reads unsigned, on origin trust; a signed card stays owed. The floor read by release (`W26` slice 4) adds one rung and closes nothing here: a browser holding the Nexus AID verifies the epoch lineage, the head release and the floor bytes itself (`browser-floor-read`), anchored to the AID alone, since the genesis epoch re-derives it. The lineage rides the release record and the porch answer, never the card (a card holds 4096 characters, and the lineage self-certifies); that carrier changes nothing about trust, because the AID that anchors it comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins and never from the answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`floor-answer.test`). The AID itself still rides the same-origin trust line, and nothing proves the card's freshness: the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed for anchoring the AID and the card. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:513:* `W15` A floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key re-files only on restart (`admit-gate-pin.ts`, `place-floor-pin.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:514:* `W16` Two-vault carry: the carry partials land no floor pin, so a cofounded Nexus carries no herm yet (`nexus-contract.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:525:* `W29` The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL (#/rulings, the place signs by a scoped signer, 2026-10-19; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane">>): built, PR #98, 2026-10-26. One KEL grammar (`vessel-kel.ts`, beside `persona-kel` and `handle-kel`): the inception seats the online signer and commits a cold next-key digest; a rotation reveals that key, which signs it, seats a replacement signer and commits a fresh next key; no interaction events. Every founding door, node, hearth, herm kindle and browser alike, mints the armed inception and lands no byte before the founding card reads back through the `PlaceFoundingCard` port, and the cold seed rests on no file. `lares vessel rotate` runs the card ceremony: it verifies the old card against the head, reads the replacement card back, then stages, publishes and reconciles under one custody claim, and a restart never invents a successor. Peers learn the head from the Nexus carriage board and an offline herm from the carry bundle; one fold, bounded at 64 rows and 8 pieces of fork evidence per AID, refuses a gap, a rollback and a fork. The five floor duties sign and verify `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`. A seed census names every raw-seed consumer and fails on a new one. Owed: a browser ceremony UI that seats a card (until it lands, the browser's KEL door refuses by name and a browser leaf holds no place KEL); the duty verifiers resolving their signer at the head (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`), with `W14`–`W16`; the seed's other reach, K15's bonds, named in the census. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:531:!! Stride 3 Bake
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:535:!!! Seven-league stride notes
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:537:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:539:* ''Integrity owed: the habit flip at the bake'' (`X0`, `G37`). Before the bake the house runs re-genesis freely, since no CRDT document survives; after it, a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins. Its witness: a census of each instrument, fixture, brief and runbook line that assumes a free re-genesis, each named to flip or retire inside the bake's own commit, never after it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:541:!!! The rows
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:545:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; built with `W29`, whose readiness red reads a fresh genesis founded armed, the five framed pairs verifying, and an old-shape inception refused by name, `old-shape-inception`), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:551:!! After The Seat
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:555:!!! Seven-league stride notes
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:559:!!! The rows
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:573:* `A12` An unlock spends its time in three boots of the wiki engine, and the terminal shows nothing meanwhile. One instrumented run on a marked scratch root, pinned to one core, with the genesis corpus alone: the key derivation takes under two seconds; the sovereign composition then takes about six to reach `corpus-ready`, seven from the `[dyad]` line to the daemon island's `working layer attached`, and four to `tw5-booted`. An unlock sent while the floor's own daemon island still boots waits that boot out first, six seconds more, so the first unlock after a restart answered in twenty-eight seconds where a later one answered in fifteen. The span a person met past eighty seconds sits at the same `[dyad]` line, so it scales with the corpus the daemon island boots over. No small cure reads here. Owed: a progress line per phase at the unlocking terminal, and a measurement over a full workspace corpus. The compose owner's boot path. A.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:576:* `K13` The sealed outbox (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Parcels rest sealed under random names in the `outbox` class. Owed: carriage shipping, idempotent receipt and local delete after ship. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:577:* `K14` The restored face's provisional standing (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>). The mark, guardian or chair view, confirm verbs and three authority-changing refusals stand. Owed: provisional guards at the root-signed crossing, edge kapae, device admit, two-founder act and session signer's authority purpose; a sibling view needs independent proof; the guardians' recovery path where every party stays unreachable. K, W, N.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:584:* `W10` The knock tests offline for a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): CLOSED as a named leak by the operator's ruling (2026-10-26), the sovereign route's promise leaving a pin-holding path reader outside it (face-proof #/named-leaks; the reading at `docs/pono/w28-gate-lane` #/the-knock-reading). More research owed later: whether a secret selector, its first-dial bootstrap and its causal re-key on every removal earn their cost, read again when a sovereign pin escapes its members' custody, when route confidentiality against pin-holders enters the promise, or when hearths commonly stand many Nexuses behind one address; a flip after `X0` moves the dial's URL bytes by its own versioned rite. W, canon.
