its spawn (`packages/lararium-node/src/worker-handle.ts`), a wiki island reaches the fetch door alone while its custody write and its rest ask refuse by name and its dyad ask draws `aside`, and a session island reaches no vessel door. A command that acts with no vessel standing opens its own key session at the first sealed row it touches (`packages/lares-cli/src/offline-custody.ts`): a terminal prompt, and under a marked scratch root the published test route. A sealed row's act rides an `act` frame of the custody door and never a store verb: one typed table bounds the acts (`packages/lararium-node/src/sealed-acts.ts`), a standing vessel answers with no second prompt, and beside a standing vessel a command opens no key session of its own, while a root's recovery split refuses there (`packages/lares-cli/src/sealed-act-door.ts`). The fleet mirror of a pet-name and a declared Handle rides that door too: `selves.carry` names a face and which name, the vessel's main thread reads the name off its sealed row and writes it onto that face's own persona plane and no other face's, only where that plane's rest seals (a clear rest refuses the carry and the name stays on its row), `lares persona sync` fills and never replaces, and no verb takes or answers a face's own name (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
