    27	
    28	''What this carrier holds.'' The build order from today's worker-thread TiddlyWiki (one engine per island, whole HTML frames to a shadow root, a render-id relay back) to the full model `dreamdom` carries: four layers, two waists, a camera as a root over a sink, a width dial, a Wiki Actor, and every surface of the superset publishing its own conformance row. Each phase names what it builds, what it proves, what it waits on, the spikes that gate it and the rulings that block it. Landed work will read in git and the CHANGELOG, never here; this carrier keeps only what stays owed, and the controller trues it as rows close.
    29	
    30	''How it rides the house roadmap.'' `stable-founding-road#/the-attractor` names STABLE FOUNDING as the attractor and rules that ''full models land early'': a slice builds its whole model in the place the order gives it, and no slice ships a narrower interim a later slice must re-cut. This train obeys that: the camera contract lands with its per-key revisions, mount epochs, answered events and declared cancellation whole, even where its first key stays the whole surface. The train runs ''beside'' the six paths of `stable-founding-road#/the-road` on disjoint files: it touches `packages/lararium-tw5/`, `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`, the island protocol's wiki kinds and the house plugin, and it leaves the compose hunks of `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` to their named owners, reaching them only through a module boundary and a patch to the owning lane. Where it needs a session shape (`session:surface-open`, the holder protocol), it builds against `session-contract` as ONE FACE lands it and refuses by name until then.
