   147	!! The spikes ~ each gating a phase, each a day to a week, each outside the tracked tree
   148	
   149	# ''Declared cancellation in one afternoon'' (D1): the `data-lar-on` and `data-lar-cancel` table for `$link`, `$button`, `$keyboard`, `$dropzone`, `$droppable`, `$browse`, `$checkbox`, `$radio`, `$select`, `$edit-text`, `$range`; click bubbling to the first listener with `unclaimed`; Playwright: an external link opens, a native checkbox toggles, the file picker opens.
   150	# ''Serializer promotion'' (D1): `checked` and `selected` properties to attributes at flush; the radio paints, the select holds.
   151	# ''Sensed revision end to end'' (D1): `localRev` on `sense`, `sensedRevision` in the frame, the `beforeNodeMorphed` veto; type, hold the answer, deliver an older frame, read the value, caret, focus, undo and the wiki's field; under focus, blur, composition and a `<select>`.
   152	# ''The seam engine's toolbar'' (D1): render the stock toolbar through the third engine, run all ten text operations over a carried pair, list which refuse `selection-unavailable`.
   153	# ''Declared keys and the document leg'' (D1): `data-lar-keys` from `parseKeyDescriptors`, real `key` and `code`, a `shortcuts` key; search Enter, tag-picker Enter, one global shortcut.
   154	# ''`import-offer` and `drop`'' (D1): page-side parse of `text/vnd.tiddler`, bounded bytes, `$:/Import` parks and performs.
   155	# ''Surface switch with epochs'' (D1): `lar:resend`, `mountEpoch` on acts, an act with an old epoch answers `stale-target`.
   156	# ''A blocks sink over a recording document'' (D2): a ~400-line document implementation that records nodes and bound listeners; render the teacher fixture's `GettingStarted` and one `$list`-bearing tiddler to `blocks`, `text` and `label-html`; a missing camera degrades visibly; interaction goldens 1, 2, 6 and 11 at parity with the DOM sink.
   157	# ''The three-boot width spike'' (D3; the separating experiment of `docs/pono/third-ways-scout` §10): one corpus, one loopback port, widths full, skinny and none, the measures and thresholds of D3 above; the fourth boot, story, only if skinny and full split.
   158	# ''The full-width walk of the five sites'' (D3): the glass engine over `window.document` inside the shadow root; `FramedEngine`, storyviews, popup positioning, the toolbar and auto-height each exercised once in a real browser before the default width gets ruled.
   159	# ''Hibernate and wake'' (D4): an actor with two attached ports hibernates, wakes, both resume at their cursors with their widths and mounts; a third port opened during hibernation triggers the wake; a port without `sensoria` sending a percept reads `refused: cap sensoria`.
